{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","soma"],"title":"Cittā","html":"<article id='thig2.5'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Therīgāthā 2.5 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Nuns 2.5 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Bhikkhunīs </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Chapter of the Twos </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cittātherīgāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cittā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Cittā </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kiñcāpi khomhi kisikā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Even though I’m skinny, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>“I was skin and bones, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>gilānā bāḷhadubbalā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>sick, and very feeble, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>sick, and very weak; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Daṇḍamolubbha gacchāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I climb the mountain, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>but, leaning on a stick, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pabbataṁ abhirūhiya. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>leaning on a staff. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>I climbed the mountain. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅghāṭiṁ nikkhipitvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having laid down my outer robe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>I laid down the outer robe </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pattakañca nikujjiya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and overturned my bowl, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>and overturned the bowl; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sele khambhesimattānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>propping myself against a rock, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>settled on a stone, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tamokhandhaṁ padāliyā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I shattered the mass of darkness. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>I destroyed this mass of darkness.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Cittā therī …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>The Elder Cittā </span></p></article>"}
